Hi Giancarlo,

Thank you for replying!

1. I am looking at the occupancy of a small-medium sized mammal. 120 cameras were set across an agricultural landscape in different types of habitat for 4 weeks in summer and winter. The bait was hung from a tree in a PVC canister with a blank cd attached. When the cameras and bait were collected the only thing that affected the bait was it was either pulled off a the tree or the contents were covered in mould, apart from that they remained intact, and whole. My only assumption is that the smell of the bait may have decreased, although just by looking at pictures, animals were still very interested in the canister...I was given the suggestion of running models with days as a covariate and keeping occupancy constant to see if detection was affected, would you agree?

2. I am also wondering whether a multi season is appropriate, however I am assuming that due to drastic changes in weather, the availability of food would change and therefore affect occupancy. Is summer vs winter not appropriate for this?

Cheers

